{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985023-homebrew-system","id":985023,"title":"Homebrew system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-10T13:13:03-07:00","id":985023,"title":"Homebrew system","content":"I've been working on a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19qgldbpr75f7iuC97ELCwWk4vSKTrNnj9ayFvOr7A2Q/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew system</a>, and I would appreciate another set of eyes on it to see if it's actually easy to break the game, I'm going to be playtesting it later today as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:32:18-07:00","id":985034,"title":"","content":"Nice start. I think I see what you're trying to do, but I don't want to assume. What is your goal here?<br /> <br /> Without really digging and trying to actively break it I couldn't see any initial flaws.<br /> <br /> I am not quite understanding the potency thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2900,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","user":"frostbyte000jm","date":".  edit, I saw something. 10-10-2016, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:40:38-07:00","id":985042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985023-homebrew-system?p=985034#post985034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice start. I think I see what you're trying to do, but I don't want to assume. What is your goal here?<br /> <br /> Without really digging and trying to actively break it I couldn't see any initial flaws.<br /> <br /> I am not quite understanding the potency thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>My goal is to take some of CofD's advances and put them in Mage the Ascension. For instance, lower dicepools, making extended rituals less obnoxious, and things of that nature.<br /> <br /> With Potency, it determines how much damage the spell heals if it's a healing spell, how much it damages if it's a damaging spell, and things of that nature. If the target is resisting, it's decreased by the target's resistance attribute; so if you're trying to throw them off their game, it would do poise, whereas if you're trying to hurt them it's based on Vitality. When determining how much Potency you have, it's equal to the penalty you put towards Potency.<br /> <br /> Are you understanding now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:54:11-07:00","id":985088,"title":"","content":"is the only way to increase potency is to take extra turns? or is that and this or that thing? like I can get two potency if I take 2 turns OR I can just take a -2 on my roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T15:07:33-07:00","id":985095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985023-homebrew-system?p=985088#post985088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is the only way to increase potency is to take extra turns? or is that and this or that thing? like I can get two potency if I take 2 turns OR I can just take a -2 on my roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so you have a base of Arete+Sphere. You can then take up to Arete+Sphere+Foci-1 in penalties. You can assign your penalties between the various spell factors. One of those is Potency. For every one penalty that you spend on Potency, the Potency increases by one. Got it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T15:41:31-07:00","id":985104,"title":"","content":"I think so, can you give me an example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:16:46-07:00","id":985115,"title":"","content":"Bob casts a Forces spell. Bob has Forces 3 Arete 3. Bob takes a penalty of two from potency. His spell's potency is now two. He has four dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:28:56-07:00","id":985119,"title":"","content":"It seems like it's pretty skewed for Technocracy, which is fine, but you should probably be clear about that up front. Backgrounds like &quot;Cloaking&quot; and &quot;Hypercram&quot; have non Technocratic terminologies (Arcane and Dream), just to name a couple. <br /> <br /> I don't see why you'd need to come up with totally new Attributes, especially since you're modeling after CoD/Awakening. I recommend starting with their basic character sheet and modify as needed. There are a few custom sheets out there for homebrew systems that involve systems from oWoD and CoD. I actually really like their system, and think that their basic play system can be used separately from the magick system, which could be modified and homebrewed independently. <br /> <br /> You'll probably also need to address your Spheres, especially since you're breaking up Entropy to Death and Fate, which is a controversial topic around these parts. Personally, I think that Entropy works better as a Sphere in the oWoD setting as written, where Fate and Death work in Awakening, as they were both built from the ground up. You start running into problems in Ascension when you start seeing crossovers of Death into the Spirit and Forces Spehres that the Arcana in Awakening avoid by designing them differently. There's also a problem with Death not having a Technocratic equivalent.<br /> <br /> That's all I have from my first cursory reading. I'll take another look later after work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:36:54-07:00","id":985121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985023-homebrew-system?p=985119#post985119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like it's pretty skewed for Technocracy, which is fine, but you should probably be clear about that up front. Backgrounds like &quot;Cloaking&quot; and &quot;Hypercram&quot; have non Technocratic terminologies (Arcane and Dream), just to name a couple.<br /> <br /> I don't see why you'd need to come up with totally new Attributes, especially since you're modeling after CoD/Awakening. I recommend starting with their basic character sheet and modify as needed. There are a few custom sheets out there for homebrew systems that involve systems from oWoD and CoD. I actually really like their system, and think that their basic play system can be used separately from the magick system, which could be modified and homebrewed independently.<br /> <br /> You'll probably also need to address your Spheres, especially since you're breaking up Entropy to Death and Fate, which is a controversial topic around these parts. Personally, I think that Entropy works better as a Sphere in the oWoD setting as written, where Fate and Death work in Awakening, as they were both built from the ground up. You start running into problems in Ascension when you start seeing crossovers of Death into the Spirit and Forces Spehres that the Arcana in Awakening avoid by designing them differently. There's also a problem with Death not having a Technocratic equivalent.<br /> <br /> That's all I have from my first cursory reading. I'll take another look later after work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just the version I copypasta'd<br /> <br /> Because I feel the StoryPath Attributes are better<br /> <br /> I'm not breaking Entropy to Death and Fate. Just renaming it and adding some more Fate stuff to it. Death is a separate thing, used almost solely by the Hollow Ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:12:28-07:00","id":985302,"title":"","content":"Are penalties spreadable over several rounds?<br /> Or is it intended that you need a lot of foci to cast something big?<br /> <br /> I like the mana/quint split.<br /> <br /> Problematic is IMO the connection inbetween enlightenment/arete and a background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:53:02-07:00","id":986220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985023-homebrew-system?p=985302#post985302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are penalties spreadable over several rounds?<br /> Or is it intended that you need a lot of foci to cast something big?<br /> <br /> I like the mana/quint split.<br /> <br /> Problematic is IMO the connection inbetween enlightenment/arete and a background.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can spread the foci over several rounds, but not the penalties.<br /> <br /> Sadly I can't take credit for the mana quint split, as that's MJ12commando's work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:42:04-07:00","id":989491,"title":"","content":"Does anyone want to spend some time creating/converting Wonders, and Talismans and shit into <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19qgldbpr75f7iuC97ELCwWk4vSKTrNnj9ayFvOr7A2Q/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">my system</a>? If you are open up chat in the doc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:55:48-07:00","id":990442,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As food for thought, in this system things like Do and True Faith aren't merits or skills. They're Enhancements. Enhancement's aren't just for Technocrats anymore, allowing for epic transhuman battles.</span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}